# P18-V01 EndTransactionRequestHeader reflection decoding — 2026-10-18T00:41:04Z

- Repository: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`.
- Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`.
- Pinned Java oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1 at
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9` in the read-only checkout
  `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/3rd/rocketmq`.
- Source inspection confirmed `EndTransactionRequestHeader` does not use
  `FastCodesHeader`. Java's reflection decoder catches each field conversion
  or missing-`@CFNotNull` error independently, then calls `checkFields()`;
  only commit states 0, 8, and 12 pass. `fromTransactionCheck` defaults to
  false, invalid Boolean text maps to false, and nullable wrappers/strings stay
  unset when absent or malformed.
- Rust now represents nullable offsets, commit state, and message ID as
  `Option`, skips per-field numeric conversion failures, applies Java Boolean
  parsing, and validates commit state after decoding. Producer transaction
  paths, protocol/remoting fixtures and tests were updated. Fixture SHA-256:
  `78605a0c0cd70f33553813559e2e6b4c9fe82589a08acd83ca18a9ebc616ab5d`.
- Code commit: `0961d24d fix(protocol): match end-transaction reflection decode`.

