## Corrections made during this slice

- An initial header validation-matrix run still expected strict required-field
  failures; it was updated to match Java's per-field reflection catch behavior.
- The generic integer-boundary matrix also assumed any valid-width integer was
  a valid enum. It now checks the Java commit-state set separately.
- Clippy identified duplicate validation branches; those were consolidated.
- An early Maven verify found fixture drift because the generator had not been
  recompiled after source edits. Regenerating with `mvn compile exec:java` and
  rerunning verify passed.

